{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-aeb2b1c048633736","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The commit introduces 4 files: .gitignore (modified, +node_modules/), package-lock.json, package.json, test/package.test.cjs. No harness junk. No secrets.\n\nWait — the task said \"only scaffold files (package.json, test/…) may be present\". .gitignore and package-lock.json are also present. package-lock.json is a legitimate lockfile that comes with a pinned devDependency (turbo) — it's standard npm hygiene and contains no secrets. The .gitignore addition of node_modules/ is standard. Neither is harness junk, a secret, or a .env file. The parenthetical \"(package.json, test/…)\" suggests scaffold files in general. The lockfile pins turbo 2.10.11, satisfying \"turbo 2.x\". I'll note this but not raise it as a defect — it's consistent with the story and is a byproduct of npm install, not junk.\n\nInteresting point: the test's AC 3 only asserts the devDependency and scripts — but the AC numbering in the tests: the test labels AC 3 as \"turbo 2.x devDependency and turbo-run scripts\", which corresponds to AC 2 in the story (\"devDependencies pins turbo 2.x, and scripts define build, test, lint\"). The story's AC 3 is \"scaffold files are committed and git commands exit 0\" — the test doesn't test that (that's a commit-hygiene matter, verified manually). The task says \"assertions must correspond 1:1 with AC\". Hmm, the 4th test is labeled \"AC 3\" but actually covers story AC 2. Story AC 3 (committed and git exit 0) is not unit-testable — that's fine, it's verified by git checks. The label mismatch is a minor nitpick at most — a label, not behavior. Test coverage: AC1 → tests 2 (and 1), AC2 → tests 3 and 4. All actual values are asserted, no vacuity (tautology). The test file is executable via node --test.\n\nAlso note: the test asserts `pkg.devDependencies.turbo` equals '^2.5.0' — if the package.json changes to a different 2.x pin, the test will fail. This couples the test to the exact version string. But this is fine — the regex also enforces 2.x. Not a substantive defect.\n\nNext things to run: node --test test/package.test.cjs, check the marker file size in HEAD, exit codes of git status / git log -1 / git show HEAD:package.json, and verify that harness files don't appear in tracked commits touching the story files.\n","signature":"f250b9564dad410d8d7f949fa758aa94"}],"model":"unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":24503,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fd3a0e8c2112106","session_id":"18cab620-6240-4ed3-9b04-d218b0f3b147","uuid":"2a9b965a-c896-4d4a-a38c-0b0219bb3450","timestamp":"2026-08-20T13:09:19.316Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"code-reviewer: review committed story work"}
